1
00:00:30,000 --> 00:00:31,540
Your moves!

2
00:00:36,640 --> 00:00:39,320
It's time to duel!

3
00:01:03,740 --> 00:01:07,260
This four-way duel is
confusing. What's the score?

4
00:01:07,440 --> 00:01:11,980
Well, so far, Joey's in the lead,
followed by Yugi in second place.

5
00:01:12,140 --> 00:01:16,160
Then you got Kaiba in third, and
Merrick bringing up the reel.

6
00:01:16,380 --> 00:01:19,640
It's my move, and I summon Dark Geroid.

7
00:01:20,600 --> 00:01:21,540
Big deal.

8
00:01:21,840 --> 00:01:23,977
It's the weakest monster
on the field, Merrick.

9
00:01:24,060 --> 00:01:28,817
Little does that fool realize that my
Dark Geroid has a very powerful ability.

10
00:01:28,900 --> 00:01:30,637
As soon as it's summoned,

11
00:01:30,720 --> 00:01:34,860
it can lower the attack points
of any monster I choose by 800.

12
00:01:35,320 --> 00:01:37,960
The question is, who should I annihilate?

13
00:01:38,240 --> 00:01:43,400
If Maric attacks me, my Ring of Destruction
Trap card will be ready for him.

14
00:01:43,680 --> 00:01:47,560
Ready to blast his monster into
the next millennium, that is.

15
00:01:48,240 --> 00:01:51,520
I'm sure that Seto Kaiba
has set a trap for me.

16
00:01:51,720 --> 00:01:54,997
I'm not interested in
attacking him anyway.

17
00:01:55,080 --> 00:01:59,720
Crushing the Pharaoh is a much
more appealing choice. However,

18
00:02:00,080 --> 00:02:01,737
even with its special ability,

19
00:02:01,820 --> 00:02:05,702
my Dark Geroid isn't strong enough
to defeat his Beast of Guilfur.

20
00:02:05,820 --> 00:02:07,467
That leaves just one target.

21
00:02:08,500 --> 00:02:11,340
I'll attack Gierfried the Iron Knight.

22
00:02:11,560 --> 00:02:12,960
I saw that coming.

23
00:02:13,240 --> 00:02:15,534
And thanks to Geroid's special ability,

24
00:02:16,020 --> 00:02:19,960
your beast gets weaker by 800 points.

25
00:02:21,640 --> 00:02:22,600
You're through.

26
00:02:22,900 --> 00:02:23,800
Not quite.

27
00:02:25,080 --> 00:02:26,000
Check this out.

28
00:02:26,240 --> 00:02:28,040
Reveal face-down card.

29
00:02:28,660 --> 00:02:30,320
Go Skull Dice!

30
00:02:31,340 --> 00:02:35,180
Now your monster's points
shrink depending on what I roll.

31
00:02:35,380 --> 00:02:37,260
So you're relying on luck?

32
00:02:37,380 --> 00:02:38,497
Yeah, that's right.

33
00:02:38,580 --> 00:02:40,227
You got a problem with that?

34
00:02:42,100 --> 00:02:43,820
Yeah, it's a two.

35
00:02:44,140 --> 00:02:47,434
That means your monster's
attack points get cut in half.

36
00:02:49,320 --> 00:02:50,150
Yes!

37
00:02:51,380 --> 00:02:56,240
Time for Geerfreed to strike back
and send your Geroid back in.

38
00:02:56,800 --> 00:02:58,380
Geerfreed, take it away!

39
00:03:01,220 --> 00:03:02,240
No way!

40
00:03:02,600 --> 00:03:03,640
My monster!

41
00:03:03,880 --> 00:03:05,280
It's a mini-Geerfreed!

42
00:03:06,260 --> 00:03:07,090
Huh?

43
00:03:07,173 --> 00:03:08,003
What's going on?

44
00:03:09,700 --> 00:03:11,400
Kaiba, you did that!

45
00:03:13,140 --> 00:03:16,297
Yes, I used my face-down shrink card.

46
00:03:16,380 --> 00:03:20,580
So thanks to me, Wheeler's monster
just lost half its strength.

47
00:03:20,960 --> 00:03:23,680
Now his creature is as puny as his mind.

48
00:03:24,760 --> 00:03:28,480
Dark Geroid, destroy
Gerefreed the Iron Knight.

49
00:03:31,840 --> 00:03:33,840
I won't forget that, Kaiba.

50
00:03:34,200 --> 00:03:35,480
Mark my words.

51
00:03:36,900 --> 00:03:38,520
Stay focused, Joey.

52
00:03:38,820 --> 00:03:41,920
I can't believe that Kaiba
just helped Merrick out.

53
00:03:42,540 --> 00:03:45,377
I mean, that's about
as low as you can get.

54
00:03:45,460 --> 00:03:47,640
He's got something planned.

55
00:03:47,980 --> 00:03:48,980
Yeah, but what?

56
00:03:49,320 --> 00:03:50,300
That was great!

57
00:03:50,640 --> 00:03:53,875
My brother's timing on that
last move was just perfect.

58
00:03:54,100 --> 00:03:57,629
